# FPS Project Knowledge Workflow

- Start with `PROJECT_INDEX.md`.
- For a subsystem task, read only the matching section in:
  - `docs/knowledge/ARCHITECTURE.md`
  - `docs/knowledge/SYSTEMS.md`
  - `docs/knowledge/ASSETS_AND_CONFIG.md`
  - `docs/knowledge/RISKS_AND_GAPS.md`
- Search `docs/knowledge/generated/index.json` or run:
  `python Tools/ProjectIndex/query_index.py <terms>`
- Do not recursively read these by default:
  `Plugins/Wwise*`, `Plugins/UnLua*`, `Plugins/UEEditorMCP/Python/.venv`,
  `Content/FPS`, `Content/ShootingAI`, `Content/StarterContent`,
  `Content/SpaceshipInterior`.
- Treat C++/Lua/INI/JSON as verified text facts. Treat offline `.uasset`
  strings as hints; use live UEEditorMCP for Blueprint graph/CDO certainty.
- Before relying on the index after meaningful source/config/asset changes, run:
  `python Tools/ProjectIndex/build_index.py --check`.
- After changing core C++, Lua, Config, custom plugins, or core assets, run:
  `python Tools/ProjectIndex/build_index.py`.
- When implementation conflicts with historical `README.pdf`, current source and
  Blueprint configuration win; record deliberate architecture changes in the
  knowledge docs.
- Read `docs/knowledge/RISKS_AND_GAPS.md` before touching networking, respawn,
  armor/damage, recoil, UI navigation, hardcoded asset paths, or UGC persistence.
